@ account index, TOTP counter -> 6-digit code string
@ HOTP writes into its scratch string in place, so make sure WRK exists and is
@ big enough first: otherwise it would write over whatever object is there.
\<< \-> i c
  \<<
    MKWRK
    ACCTS i GET 2 GET c R\->B WRK
    IF DUP TYPE 2 \=/ THEN "WRK is not a string" DOERR END
    IF DUP SIZE 355 < THEN "WRK too short" DOERR END
    HOTP B\->R 1000000 MOD FMT6
  \>>
\>>
